absent_from_table:       # keep the FULL consensus-pair anchor at its CURRENT vintage.
  # The pipeline already values every name at the live prices_daily close — what
  # these four keep is the watchlist STATIC pair as one older vintage. NEVER move
  # a watchlist price against a stale pnav (the TEN $44 lesson).
  - TEN
  - SB
  - CMDB
  - GSL

issuer_sourced:            # 2343 — consensus_pnav derived from the ISSUER-published
  # fleet value (2026 Interim, 30-Jun basis), promoted 2026-08-13. The NAV anchor
  # does NOT move tonight (next re-derivation venue: AR2026 ~Mar-2027). What moves
  # is the PRICE LEG — the whole point of this sitting for 2343:
  "2343":
    nav_per_share_usd: 0.4297      # UNCHANGED (2026 Interim issuer-composite, 30-Jun)
    price_leg: >
      Promote the NEWEST HK CLOSE in prices_daily at promote time — NOT tonight's
      fetched $0.5126, which is a LIVE Wed-8/19 11:59-HKT intraday tick (the fetch
      ran during the HK morning session). At the Tue-8/18 close the print was ~$0.50;
      Wed's close will have printed by the owner sitting. Cite close + HKD FX from
      the prices_daily entry promoted in the same commit.
    pnav_rule: >
      consensus_pnav = promoted_price / 0.4297, computed at promote — never pasted
      (structural TEN-$44 protection, per the 8/13 lane rules). At ~$0.50 that is
      ~1.16 (was 0.91 at the stale $0.390): the month-long HKG rally moved the name
      from a discount to a ~16% PREMIUM over issuer-composite NAV. That is a REAL
      read change (the T/S the 8/16 ratify eyeballed), not an artifact.
    fwd_pe_rule: >
      RECOMPUTE this sitting: price / FY2026 consensus EPS US$0.03 -> ~0.50/0.03
      = ~16.7x (2-dp aggregator EPS, stockanalysis 7/14 — estimate leg unchanged).
      NOTE this DEVIATES from the 8/13 promote, which deliberately left 13.0 —
      correctly, because THAT promote held the price leg at 7/14 too (both legs one
      vintage). Tonight the price leg MOVES, so holding the old ratio would pair a
      new price with an old-price-derived P/E — the exact mixing the pair rule bans.
    static_guard_effect: >
      Re-pinning current_price ~0.50 resets the ±30% guard base — the live feed
      re-applies (tonight's flag clears at the next fetch), the static-fallback
      regime ends, and the guard means something again (fires at ~0.35 / ~0.65).

anchor_maintenance:        # GNK — the 8/13-ruled DEAL CAVEAT rewrite fires NOW
  GNK:
    what_happened: >
      Diana WITHDREW the non-binding indicative proposal 2026-08-14 (Diana release
      8/14 + Genco board letter 8/14; digest 2026-08-16 M1/M5). The re-check the
      8/13 draft registered ("either outcome re-points this field") has FIRED on
      the Diana-walks branch. The 8/24 board response date is pre-empted, moot.
    analyst_target_28_40: >
      STANDS as ruled (broker NAV basis, owner 8/13) — the basis did not die with
      the proposal; it was chosen precisely because it does not depend on the deal.
      NOTE for a future re-pin, not this promote: the 8/18 daily implies a FRESH
      Pareto NAV ~$27.0 (26.2 / 0.97) vs the pinned $28.40 (8/06 daily, 0.9x) —
      a ~5% drift. Owner may re-pin at the next GNK ruling; do not move it silently.
    caveat_rewrite: >
      REWRITE (not delete) the DEAL CAVEAT block in the watchlist comment: the tape
      is now FULLY un-pinned — no live proposal, no tender. First post-withdrawal
      close moved UP (+4.3% to $26.34 on 8/14) and EV widened to -13.9%: the
      market repriced GNK ABOVE the dead deal's implied totals, inverting the
      deal-premium-unwind intuition (digest M5; one close = thin evidence, but 8/17
      $26.2 daily print + 8/18 $26.05 close both HELD the level — confirmed, not a
      one-print artifact). Keep the band-boundary warning: GNK sits ON its band
      edge; do not read T/S prints as thesis deterioration.
    log_annotation_owed: decisions/gnk_log.md still carries NO Diana-withdrawal
      annotation — land it with this promote (drafted in the promote checklist).

